      "message": "How about moving all of these to where you have the other stubs, so the `HAVE_PRIVATE` and real implementations are better separated?\n\ne.g.,\n\n```\n#ifdef HAVE_PRIVATE\n\n// all the non-working versions\nint fp_sensor_init(void)\n{\n  return EC_ERROR_INVAL;\n \n}\n\nint fp_finger_match(void *templ, uint32_t templ_count, uint8_t *image,\n\t\t    int32_t *match_index, uint32_t *update_bitmap)\n{\n\treturn EC_ERROR_INVAL;\n}\n\n...\n\n#else\n\n// all the real versions\nint fp_sensor_init(void)\n{\n  // real logic \n}\n\nint fp_finger_match(void *templ, uint32_t templ_count, uint8_t *image,\n\t\t    int32_t *match_index, uint32_t *update_bitmap)\n{\n  // real logic\n}\n\n#endif\n\n```\n\nTaking one step further, you could move them into separate files:\n\n* `fpc_private.c`: real implementations\n* `fpc_stubs.c`: stubs for when private doesn\u0027t exist",
