      "message": "Yes, this is what I was thinking, although it would be nice to get rid of wrapping the files in `#if defined(HAVE_PRIVATE)` if possible and just build either the private version or public version depending on the build config.\n\nDoes it work if you add something like this in the `build.mk`?\n\n```\nall-obj-rw+\u003d$(libfp_cur_dir)fpc_sensor_pal.o\n\nifeq ($(HAVE_PRIVATE),y)\nall-obj-rw+\u003d$(libfp_cur_dir)fpc_private.o \nelse\nall-obj-rw+\u003d$(libfp_cur_dir)fpc_stubs.o\nendif\n```\n\nThen you could just add some guards in the source files to make sure the file is not accidentally included in the wrong build:\n\n```\n#ifndef HAVE_PRIVATE\n#error This file should only be included in the private build\n#endif\n```\n\n(and the opposite in the stubs file that should only be in the public build).",
